{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2405","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2405","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2405\",\"parent_revision\":\"f1477063999a61e16b6d3887deb224dd7572c920e0989c3bca067bdc5fd93ee6\",\"root_revision\":\"f1477063999a61e16b6d3887deb224dd7572c920e0989c3bca067bdc5fd93ee6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Planning pipeline lacks primary-source access: agents adapt from research summaries instead of fetching upstream sources\\nDate: 2026-05-22\\nGoal: Instrument add-new-feature Phase 1 (feature-researcher) and Phase 3 (architecture spec) to fetch primary source URLs from research artifact frontmatter before adapting external content, and apply the same pattern to the parallel feature-discovery skill in plugin-creator.\\nConditions:\\n1. Location of add-new-feature SKILL.md in repo | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File: plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md (confirmed exists)\\n2. Location of feature-researcher agent file | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File: plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md (confirmed exists)\\n3. Exact format of prior_artifacts block in feature-researcher delegation | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-check verified lines 110-112 contain artifact_read instruction without resource_url extraction\\n4. Research artifact frontmatter fields resource_url and github_url confirmed present | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File: research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md confirmed resource_url field at line 5 (fact-check)\\n5. Phase 3 architecture spec delegation receives research artifact context | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-check verified lines 333-340 of add-new-feature/SKILL.md contain Phase 3 delegation that reads artifacts without resource_url directive\\n6. quality_vigilance section location and content in add-new-feature SKILL.md | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Command: grep -n \\\"quality_vigilance\\\" plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md \u2192 lines 74,80,101,107,161,167,325,331,378,384,439,445,465,471 (14 injection points confirmed)\\n7. WebFetch/WebSearch tools available to feature-researcher and architecture spec agents | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-check verified mcp__Ref and mcp__exa in feature-researcher tools list; mcp__exa__web_search_exa in python-cli-design-spec\\n8. Fetch failure handling pattern in existing pipeline code | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Command: grep -n \\\"fallback\\\\|WIZARD_DECLINED\\\" add-new-feature/SKILL.md \u2192 lines 247,295 confirm suggest-mode fallback pattern (WIZARD_DECLINED \u2192 suggest mode fallback) exists as precedent\\n9. Location of parallel feature-discovery skill in plugin-creator | Snapshot: (new) \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst confirmed plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md via broadcast; file exists\\n10. feature-discovery delegation structure matches feature-researcher pattern | Snapshot: (new) \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Citation: Derivation path: read plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md Phase 1/Phase 3 delegation sections\\n11. Scope of quality_vigilance preamble usage across all agent delegations | Snapshot: (new) \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Citation: grep confirmed 14 injection points across 7 location pairs; exact per-phase mapping derivable by reading SKILL.md section headers\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 3: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (fact-checker verified lines 110-112)\\n- Condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (fact-checker verified lines 333-340)\\n- Condition 6: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (grep confirmed 14 injection points)\\n- Condition 8: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (grep confirmed WIZARD_DECLINED fallback pattern at lines 247,295)\\n- Condition 9: (new) AVAILABLE (impact-analyst scope broadcast)\\n- Condition 10: (new) DERIVABLE (feature-discovery structure not yet read)\\n- Condition 11: (new) DERIVABLE (quality_vigilance phase mapping not enumerated)\\nAVAILABLE count: 9\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSkills and features adapted from external sources inherit whatever information loss, interpretation errors, or staleness exists in the research summary layer. There is no mechanism in the current pipeline to escalate from \\\"a research entry exists about this\\\" to \\\"fetch and read the actual source before building.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md::Phase1` \u2014 Orchestrates the feature-researcher delegation. Currently passes only `artifact_read(artifact_type=\\\"research\\\")` to the agent with no instruction to extract `resource_url` from research frontmatter or follow upstream URLs. Adding a primary-source access step here is the root fix point for Phase 1. | Risk: HIGH | Why: This is the originating orchestration instruction; any downstream agent quality improvement is moot if the orchestrator does not inject the access pattern.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md::Phase3` \u2014 Architecture spec delegation. Passes research artifacts without instructing the design-spec agent to follow `resource_url` citations or perform upstream best-practices searches. No `WebSearch` directive for external pattern discovery. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Architect produces the blueprint from which all implementation tasks derive; uninformed architecture decisions propagate into every downstream task.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md::philosophy` \u2014 Defines the \\\"Training Data as Hypothesis\\\" discipline but limits the verification scope to local codebase claims (`Verify before asserting`, `Cite sources` referencing `file:line`). No directive to extract `resource_url` from research frontmatter or fetch upstream sources before writing feature-context. | Risk: HIGH | Why: This is the executing agent for Phase 1. The missing instruction creates the exact gap described in the item: the agent treats research summaries as authoritative without fetching primaries.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 Consumes `feature-context-{slug}.md` (Phase 1 output) and `architect-{slug}.md` (Phase 3 output) to produce SAM task plans. Upstream quality gap in how research is incorporated propagates directly into task decomposition quality and completeness. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: The task planner uses the outputs as inputs verbatim; if those outputs omit primary-source findings or fail to surface upstream best practices, the task plan has a foundational accuracy gap.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feature-request.md` \u2014 Builds the feature request template passed to `add-new-feature`. Passes the Impact Radius and grooming context sections. Does not include a directive to supply `resource_url` content or instruct the downstream pipeline to fetch upstream sources. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: This template shapes what context the orchestrator receives when it runs `add-new-feature`; missing primary-source data in the template means the pipeline always starts with a local-only view.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md` \u2014 Assesses information completeness. RT-ICA conditions are drawn from the Impact Radius and Fact-Check sections. If primary-source data is never fetched, conditions about upstream interface behavior or best-practice alignment will be filed as DERIVABLE (can be fetched) rather than AVAILABLE, potentially letting feature plans proceed with unresolved upstream questions. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Completeness gate may pass on incomplete information if RT-ICA conditions assume secondary summaries are sufficient primary evidence.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/fact-checker.md` \u2014 Fact-checking against primary sources is this agent's core mandate. Currently spawned by the grooming swarm (pre-planning), not by the planning pipeline (Phases 1/3). If the planning pipeline does not instruct agents to follow `resource_url`, the fact-checker's pre-planning verdicts may cover different source sets than what the feature-researcher actually used. | Risk: LOW | Why: The gap is in pipeline orchestration, not in the fact-checker agent itself; the agent already uses MCP research tools correctly.\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md` \u2014 Parallel agent in the plugin-creator plugin that performs the same feature research role as `feature-researcher` for plugin development workflows. Shares the same research methodology pattern. Does not currently include a directive to extract `resource_url` from research artifacts or fetch upstream sources. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: If the fix is applied only to `feature-researcher` but not to `feature-discovery`, plugin development workflows retain the same primary-source gap.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` \u2014 Documents the Planning phase data flow: `feature-researcher \u2192 codebase-analyzer \u2192 python-cli-design-spec`. If `resource_url` extraction and upstream fetch steps are added to Phase 1 and Phase 3, the publisher-consumer map becomes stale. | Risk: LOW | Why: Architectural diagram drift is a documentation risk, not a runtime risk; the pipeline still functions correctly.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md` \u2014 States that changes to `feature-researcher` and `python-cli-design-spec` agent prompts are out of scope. If those agent prompts are updated (as this item requires), this document's \\\"Out of scope\\\" list needs to be updated to reflect that prompt changes to those agents are now considered in scope for this type of quality improvement. | Risk: LOW | Why: Policy document drift; does not block correctness but creates misleading guidance for maintainers.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/ecosystem-researcher.md` \u2014 Parallel research agent that explicitly fetches upstream sources via MCP tools (`mcp__Ref`, `mcp__exa`, `mcp__context7`). Serves as the reference implementation for the behavior this item wants to inject into `feature-researcher`. Relevant as a pattern source. | Risk: LOW | Why: No change needed here; it already does primary-source access correctly. Useful reference for what a fixed `feature-researcher` should look like.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md::quality_vigilance block` \u2014 The shared `<quality_vigilance>` preamble includes \\\"statements of fact without citation\\\" as a check \u2014 but it scopes citation to `file:line` (local codebase). After this fix, the quality vigilance block needs to be updated to also require citations to upstream URLs when external content is adapted. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Quality vigilance is injected into all phase delegation prompts; if it does not include the upstream citation requirement, agents will continue treating local references as complete citations.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md::Agents Overview` \u2014 Lists `@dh:feature-researcher` as producing research artifacts and describes Phase 1 as \\\"discovery\\\". Does not describe any primary-source access responsibility. If the agent's role is extended, the CLAUDE.md description of its behavior should be updated. | Risk: LOW | Why: Descriptive only; no runtime impact.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/SKILL.md` \u2014 Router skill that describes `/dh:add-new-feature` as \\\"discovery \u2192 codebase analysis \u2192 architecture spec \u2192 task decomposition\\\". Does not describe primary-source access as part of discovery. Stale after this fix. | Risk: LOW | Why: Router skill is a high-level overview; updated description of discovery scope is a correctness improvement, not a blocking issue.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/default-development-flow.md` \u2014 Stage 1 (Discovery) description does not mention upstream source access as part of the discovery gate. If primary-source access becomes a required step, this document should reflect it. | Risk: LOW | Why: Architectural documentation drift.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- None identified. The planning pipeline is driven entirely by agent instruction files (SKILL.md, agent .md). No configuration files, environment variables, or CI workflows control whether `resource_url` is fetched or whether upstream sources are consulted.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md::process::Step3` \u2014 Codebase exploration step uses `Grep`, `Glob`, `Read` against local source only. No step to read research artifact frontmatter for `resource_url`, no step to call `mcp__Ref__ref_read_url`, `mcp__Ref__ref_search_documentation`, or `mcp__exa__get_code_context_exa` on upstream sources. These tools are already declared in the agent's `tools:` list but are not instructed in the process steps. | Risk: HIGH | Why: The process steps are the agent's executable instructions; having tools available without process instructions means the capability is latent but never exercised.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md::philosophy::Training Data as Hypothesis` \u2014 Instructs agents to \\\"Verify before asserting\\\" and \\\"Cite sources\\\" with `file:line` references. This philosophy section should be updated to explicitly include upstream URL verification via `resource_url` from research frontmatter as a required verification path when the feature involves external content. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Philosophy section shapes the agent's default behavior baseline for every research task; the omission causes the citation standard to stop at local sources.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md::Phase1 delegation prompt template` \u2014 Instructs the feature-researcher to read research artifacts but contains no step for extracting `resource_url` or fetching upstream content. The template needs a new step: extract `resource_url` from each research artifact's frontmatter and fetch each URL before writing the feature-context document. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Orchestrator delegation prompts are the authoritative instructions agents receive; the absence of this step means the agent will never attempt upstream access unless it infers the need independently.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md::Phase3 delegation prompt template` \u2014 Architecture spec delegation has no `WebSearch` directive for upstream best practices. Needs an explicit \\\"search for current best practices and patterns for [the domain being designed]\\\" step before writing the architect document. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Architecture decisions made without consulting upstream patterns risk being inconsistent with the current state of the ecosystem, particularly for external-tool integration features.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md::Single Item prompt` \u2014 Passes the Impact Radius section to the groomer agent but does not include a directive about primary-source access when the item references upstream tools or research. The groomer therefore cannot propagate primary-source context into the groomed item. | Risk: LOW | Why: Grooming is pre-planning; primary-source access in grooming is already partially handled by the fact-checker agent. The gap here is less severe.\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md` \u2014 Parallel implementation of feature research for plugin-creator workflows. Shares the same local-only research methodology gap. If the fix pattern (extract `resource_url`, fetch upstream, cite) is introduced to `feature-researcher`, a corresponding update should be made here for consistency. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Without updating this agent-instruction file, plugin development workflows remain unpatched.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` | Role: producer | Connection: orchestrates Phase 1 and Phase 3 delegations; delegation prompt templates are the direct source of the gap | Action: MULTIPLE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` | Role: producer | Connection: executing agent for Phase 1; process steps and philosophy section are the gap location | Action: MULTIPLE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: consumes feature-context and architect artifacts; inherits quality gap if upstreams are not fixed | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feature-request.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: builds the context template passed into add-new-feature; no primary-source context injected | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: completeness gate; may pass DERIVABLE conditions that should require primary-source verification | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/fact-checker.md` | Role: other-reference | Connection: already uses primary sources correctly; referenced as validation that the capability exists | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/ecosystem-researcher.md` | Role: other-reference | Connection: reference implementation of correct primary-source access pattern via MCP tools | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md` | Role: producer | Connection: parallel agent-instruction file for plugin-creator discovery; same gap as feature-researcher | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: publisher-consumer map will be stale after pipeline step additions | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: \\\"out of scope\\\" list references feature-researcher prompt changes; will become incorrect | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md::quality_vigilance` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: shared preamble that defines citation standard; scoped to local files only | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: describes agent responsibilities; will be stale if feature-researcher role expands | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/SKILL.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: router skill description of discovery phase | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/default-development-flow.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Stage 1 description; upstream access not mentioned | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: groomer prompt template; does not propagate primary-source directive | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Both Phase 1 and Phase 3 delegation templates are the direct source of the gap; all downstream quality issues derive from this file\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` \u2014 Process steps and philosophy section are missing the upstream fetch pattern; tools are available but no instructions exercise them\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md::quality_vigilance` \u2014 The shared citation-quality preamble scopes \\\"cite sources\\\" to local `file:line` references, actively reinforcing local-only verification for all phases\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - behavioral \u2014 agents execute correctly but produce outputs based on summaries instead of primary sources, silently degrading output quality without errors\\n  - documentation \u2014 philosophy sections and quality vigilance preambles establish local-only citation as the standard, training agents to treat this as correct behavior\\n  - scope \u2014 the gap affects not only `feature-researcher` but also the Phase 3 architect agent, the shared quality vigilance preamble, and the parallel `feature-discovery` agent in a different plugin\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md` not in original description \u2014 parallel implementation with the same gap in a different plugin\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md::quality_vigilance` not in original description \u2014 shared preamble injected into all phases that actively limits citation scope to local files, expanding the fix surface beyond just Phase 1 and Phase 3 delegation templates\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible (`add-new-feature/SKILL.md` Phase 1 + Phase 3 delegation templates)\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible (`swarm-task-planner`, `rtica-assessor`, `feature-request.md` template)\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added (no automated tests identified for agent instruction behavior \u2014 verification gap noted)\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated (`workflow-architecture-diagram.md`, `plan-artifact-lifecycle.md`, `default-development-flow.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `development-harness/SKILL.md`)\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated (None identified)\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated (`feature-researcher.md` process + philosophy, `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` quality_vigilance preamble, `plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md`)\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved (not applicable \u2014 this is a behavioral gap, not a migration)\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked (Phase 4 `swarm-task-planner` and Phase 5 task workers inherit quality gap transitively; verified that quality gate agents (`plan-validator`, `feature-verifier`) do not override or compensate for upstream research quality)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: **ALIGNED**\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n0 concerns identified \u2014 proposed change is consistent with product mission and historical direction.\\n\\n### Rationale\\n\\nThe proposed change to add URL-fetching from research artifact frontmatter (`resource_url`, `github_url`) into Phase 1 (feature-researcher) and Phase 3 (architecture spec) of the `add-new-feature` skill, and to extend `quality_vigilance` to cover external URLs, is **directly aligned** with three foundational aspects of the development-harness product design:\\n\\n#### 1. **Aligns with Core Mission: \\\"Evidence Discipline\\\"**\\n\\nThe DH plugin CLAUDE.md (line 19) declares: *\\\"Task complexity is context-fit under uncertainty\\\"* and references the Layer 0 design principles including \\\"evidence discipline.\\\" The proposed change operationalizes evidence discipline by requiring agents to:\\n- Fetch primary sources before adapting research summaries\\n- Verify source currency and completeness  \\n- Apply citation discipline to external URLs (not just local file:line references)\\n\\nThis strengthens the harness's commitment to observable facts over assumptions and to treating training data and summaries as hypotheses requiring verification.\\n\\n#### 2. **Aligns with Design Principle: \\\"Every Stage Produces MCP-Registered Artifacts\\\"**\\n\\nCurrent design (CLAUDE.md lines 16-17): *\\\"Every stage produces an MCP-registered artifact (stateless handoff) \u2014 stored via artifact_register and retrieved via artifact_read, never via direct filesystem paths.\\\"*\\n\\nThe proposed change:\\n- Requires agents to extract `resource_url` from research artifact frontmatter (honoring the artifact structure already in place)\\n- Instructs agents to fetch and validate upstream sources before composing output artifacts\\n- Ensures downstream consumers (swarm-task-planner, architects) receive research that has been validated against primary sources\\n\\nThis maintains the MCP-native artifact pattern while strengthening the quality of artifacts passed between stages.\\n\\n#### 3. **Aligns with Historical Direction: Quality Vigilance and Verification**\\n\\nRecent merged commits show active investment in quality gates and verification:\\n- `beb152c` (2026-05-21): Added Section 8 (observations, gaps, backlog capture) to verify-done\\n- `83e5ac8` (2026-05-21): Implemented `dh:multi-perspective-review` skill\\n- `6d3e770` (2026-04-30): Added ripgrep-based blast-radius enumeration to feasibility-gate\\n- `30012e5` through `73903ad` (2026-05-10\u20132026-05-21): Multiple refactors to backlog protocol and artifact handling\\n\\nThe pattern is systematic strengthening of evidence quality and verification rigor. The proposed change extends this direction into the research and discovery phases by requiring primary-source validation.\\n\\n#### 4. **Does NOT Violate Any Dispatch Pattern Rule**\\n\\nThe change affects agent instruction files (`feature-researcher.md`, `add-new-feature/SKILL.md`) and skill delegation templates, not the orchestration dispatch routing. It does not:\\n- Route to `general-purpose` instead of `dh:task-worker` (Dispatch Pattern rule violated)\\n- Bypass the `dh:task-worker` universal dispatcher (no routing changes)\\n- Store artifacts via filesystem path instead of MCP (maintains artifact_register pattern)\\n- Add arbitrary human checkpoints outside ARL (adds agent-level verification, not orchestrator gates)\\n\\n#### 5. **Scope Extension to `plugin-creator:feature-discovery` Is Within Mission Scope**\\n\\nThe item description extends the fix to `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md`. This is appropriate because:\\n- Feature-discovery is the parallel research agent in the plugin-creator plugin\\n- It performs the identical role (feature research for plugin development workflows) with the same local-only methodology gap\\n- Layer 1 of the SDLC (language plugin design, CLAUDE.md lines 398-399) establishes that language plugins adopt harness patterns for consistency\\n- Extending the fix across both plugins (dh and plugin-creator) demonstrates the principle that quality improvements apply uniformly across the harness ecosystem\\n\\nThis is NOT scope creep \u2014 it is consistent application of a quality principle across plugins that share the same agent role.\\n\\n#### 6. **Quality Vigilance Extension Is Not a Design Violation**\\n\\nThe proposed change to extend `quality_vigilance` (shared preamble in `add-new-feature/SKILL.md`) to require citations to upstream URLs when external content is adapted:\\n- Strengthens the existing quality vigilance discipline (which already requires \\\"statements of fact without citation\\\" checking)\\n- Expands citation scope from local-only (`file:line`) to include external sources (`resource_url`)\\n- Ensures consistency across all phases that use the shared preamble\\n\\nThis is an **refinement** of an existing design principle, not a violation of it.\\n\\n### Conclusion\\n\\nThe proposed change is **ALIGNED** with the development-harness product mission because it:\\n1. Operationalizes the stated commitment to evidence discipline and observable facts\\n2. Respects the MCP-native artifact handling pattern\\n3. Continues a documented historical direction of strengthening verification and quality gates\\n4. Respects dispatch pattern rules and does not add arbitrary checkpoints\\n5. Applies harness principles consistently across plugins\\n6. Refines existing quality discipline rather than introducing new constraints\\n\\nThe change is a **quality improvement to the pipeline**, not a mission divergence.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-22)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nThe gap manifests on every execution of the `add-new-feature` pipeline when the backlog item being worked has one or more research artifacts (files under `research/`) whose frontmatter contains a `resource_url` or `github_url` field. The condition is deterministic, not flaky:\\n\\n1. A research artifact exists for the feature (e.g., `research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md`).\\n2. The artifact's YAML frontmatter contains `resource_url:` pointing to an upstream primary source.\\n3. The `add-new-feature` Phase 1 delegation fires and the feature-researcher agent reads the artifact via `artifact_read(artifact_type=\\\"research\\\")`.\\n4. The agent produces a `feature-context-{slug}.md` output that adapts from the research summary without having fetched the URL at `resource_url`.\\n5. Inspection of the feature-context artifact shows no content derived from the primary source beyond what appeared in the local summary.\\n\\nObservation conditions confirmed by fact-check (2026-05-22):\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 110-112: Phase 1 delegation contains no directive to extract or follow `resource_url`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` lines 85-86: Citation discipline scopes to `file:line` only.\\n- Instance observed in production: backlog item #2241 (codemod-runner skill), where agents adapted from `research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md` without fetching `resource_url` or `github_url`.\\n\\nThe gap applies equally to Phase 3 (architecture spec) when the Phase 3 delegation receives research artifacts without a WebSearch directive for upstream best practices.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nEffort: Medium (see Effort section)\\nPriority: P2 (7/10)\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 P2 is appropriate.\\n\\nRationale:\\n- The gap silently degrades the quality of every feature built from a research artifact that references an external source. Output is not broken \u2014 it is subtly incomplete, inheriting whatever information loss, interpretation errors, or staleness existed at the time the research summary was written.\\n- The risk is cumulative and non-obvious. A skill or feature built on a stale summary does not fail visibly at build time; the deficiency surfaces when the skill is used and found to be missing edge cases or examples that were present in the upstream source.\\n- The blast radius is HIGH: affects Phase 1 (feature-researcher), Phase 3 (architect), the shared quality_vigilance preamble injected into all phases, and a parallel agent in a separate plugin (plugin-creator:feature-discovery).\\n- Severity is mitigated from P1 because: (1) agents do produce working output \u2014 the gap is quality, not correctness; (2) the capability to fetch upstream sources is already present in the agent tool lists (mcp__Ref, mcp__exa) \u2014 it is only the instruction that is absent; (3) no data loss occurs.\\n- Blocking impact is present: the RT-ICA completeness assessor (rtica-assessor) may classify DERIVABLE conditions that should require AVAILABLE primary-source verification, allowing feature plans to proceed on incomplete foundations.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **Skills and features built from research artifacts**: inherit information loss and staleness from the research summary layer without any signal that the primary source was not consulted. The resulting outputs may omit structure, examples, edge cases, or breaking changes present in the upstream source.\\n- **Architecture decisions in Phase 3**: are made without consulting the current state of the upstream ecosystem. For external-tool integration features (the most common case for research-backed features), this means design choices may be inconsistent with the upstream library's current API or best practices.\\n- **RT-ICA completeness gate**: conditions about upstream interface behavior or best-practice alignment are classified as DERIVABLE (can be fetched later) rather than AVAILABLE, allowing feature plans to proceed with unresolved upstream questions.\\n- **swarm-task-planner (Phase 4)**: consumes the feature-context and architect artifacts as inputs verbatim. If those artifacts omit primary-source findings, the resulting SAM task plans have a foundational accuracy gap that propagates into every downstream implementation task.\\n- **plugin-creator plugin workflows**: share the identical gap via `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md` \u2014 fixing only the `dh` plugin leaves plugin development workflows unpatched.\\n- **Citation standard is actively reinforced as local-only**: the `quality_vigilance` preamble injected into all phase delegation prompts scopes \\\"Cite sources\\\" to `file:line` references, training all pipeline agents to treat local cites as complete citations.\\n\\nBottleneck: `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 both Phase 1 and Phase 3 delegation templates are the originating instruction source. All downstream quality issues derive from this file's silence on `resource_url` extraction.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Features and skills built from research-backed pipelines reflect the actual state of upstream sources at the time of implementation, not the state at the time the research summary was written.\\n- Architecture decisions in Phase 3 are grounded in current upstream best practices rather than potentially stale summaries, reducing the likelihood of building against an outdated API or missing a breaking change.\\n- The `quality_vigilance` citation standard becomes coherent across both local and external sources \u2014 agents no longer have an implicit permission to stop verifying at the local file boundary.\\n- The RT-ICA completeness gate can distinguish between conditions that are genuinely AVAILABLE (primary source has been fetched and verified) and conditions that are DERIVABLE (could be fetched but have not been), improving the signal quality of completeness assessments.\\n- The pattern aligns the `dh` plugin's discovery phase with the behavior already implemented in `ecosystem-researcher.md`, which correctly fetches upstream sources via MCP tools (`mcp__Ref`, `mcp__exa`, `mcp__context7`) \u2014 the fix makes the behavior consistent rather than agent-specific.\\n- Applying the same fix to `plugin-creator:feature-discovery` closes the gap uniformly across both development pipelines, avoiding a divergence where `dh` workflows get primary-source access but plugin development workflows do not.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen the `add-new-feature` pipeline runs for a feature whose backlog item has associated research artifacts:\\n\\n1. The feature-context artifact produced at the end of Phase 1 contains findings that can be traced to primary upstream sources \u2014 not only to the local research summary. Where a research artifact's frontmatter contains a `resource_url` or `github_url`, the feature-context reflects content from that URL.\\n\\n2. The architecture artifact produced at the end of Phase 3 references current upstream best practices for the domain being designed. Where external patterns were consulted, the artifact cites the upstream source explicitly.\\n\\n3. The `quality_vigilance` citation standard, when observed in Phase 1 and Phase 3 outputs, applies to external source URLs and not only to local `file:line` references. An agent output that adapts external content without citing the upstream source is flagged as a quality violation.\\n\\n4. The RT-ICA assessment for a feature involving external sources marks upstream interface conditions as AVAILABLE (primary source fetched and reviewed) rather than DERIVABLE, reflecting that the agent has actually obtained the upstream data.\\n\\n5. The behavior is consistent across `dh:add-new-feature` and `plugin-creator` workflows \u2014 both research phases access upstream sources using the same pattern.\\n\\nThe reference implementation for this observable behavior already exists in `plugins/development-harness/agents/ecosystem-researcher.md`, which fetches upstream sources via MCP tools as part of its standard process.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Run `add-new-feature` for a backlog item that has a research artifact with `resource_url` in its frontmatter. Inspect the resulting `feature-context-{slug}.md` artifact. It contains content that can only have originated from the primary source URL \u2014 not from the local research summary alone. The artifact cites the upstream URL explicitly.\\n\\n2. Grep `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` for the string `resource_url`. At least one match appears in the Phase 1 delegation prompt context, confirming the instruction to extract and follow upstream URLs is present in the orchestrator template.\\n\\n3. Grep `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` for a directive referencing `resource_url` or `mcp__Ref__ref_read_url` or equivalent upstream fetch instruction. At least one match appears in the process steps section (not only in the tools list).\\n\\n4. Grep `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` for the `quality_vigilance` block. The block contains a citation requirement that applies to external URLs or upstream sources \u2014 not only to local `file:line` references.\\n\\n5. Grep `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` for a WebSearch or upstream best-practices directive in the Phase 3 delegation prompt. At least one match appears indicating the architect agent is expected to consult current external patterns.\\n\\n6. Grep `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md` for a `resource_url` or upstream fetch directive. At least one match appears, confirming the gap has been closed in the plugin-creator pipeline as well.\\n\\n7. Read `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` lines covering the \\\"Training Data as Hypothesis\\\" philosophy section. The section explicitly includes upstream URL verification (via `resource_url` from research frontmatter) as a required verification path \u2014 not only local `file:line` citation.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Reference implementation | `plugins/development-harness/agents/ecosystem-researcher.md` \u2014 already fetches upstream sources via `mcp__Ref`, `mcp__exa`, `mcp__context7`; the behavioral pattern to replicate in feature-researcher |\\n| Research artifact with upstream URLs | `research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md` \u2014 the concrete example from #2241 where `resource_url` and `github_url` were present but unused |\\n| Primary gap location | `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Phase 1 (lines 110-112), Phase 3 (lines 333-340), quality_vigilance (lines 101-107) |\\n| Agent with gap | `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` \u2014 process Step 3 and philosophy section (lines 73-87) |\\n| Parallel gap | `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md` \u2014 same missing directive in plugin-creator workflows |\\n| Consumer template | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feature-request.md` |\\n| MCP tools available (already in agent tool lists) | `mcp__Ref__ref_read_url`, `mcp__Ref__ref_search_documentation`, `mcp__exa__get_code_context_exa`, `mcp__exa__web_search_exa` |\\n| Prior art (backlog item #2241) | Codemod-runner skill implementation \u2014 the observed instance of the gap in production |\\n| Skill | /dh:add-new-feature |\\n| Agent | @dh:feature-researcher |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nFiles that need changes (from Impact Radius \u2014 HIGH and MEDIUM risk items with actions other than VERIFY_COMPATIBLE):\\n\\n**Agent instructions \u2014 HIGH risk (missing upstream fetch directive):**\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Phase 1 delegation prompt template (lines 110-112), Phase 3 delegation prompt template (lines 333-340), and shared `quality_vigilance` preamble (lines 101-107)\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` \u2014 process Step 3 (codebase exploration, no upstream fetch step) and philosophy \\\"Training Data as Hypothesis\\\" section (lines 73-87, citation scoped to local only)\\n\\n**Agent instructions \u2014 MEDIUM risk (parallel gap in second plugin):**\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/plugin-creator/skills/feature-discovery/SKILL.md` \u2014 same local-only research methodology gap as feature-researcher\\n\\n**Consumer templates \u2014 MEDIUM risk (no primary-source context injected):**\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/feature-request.md` \u2014 context template passed into add-new-feature; does not supply `resource_url` content or a directive to fetch upstream sources\\n\\n**Documentation \u2014 LOW risk (stale after pipeline changes):**\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md`\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md`\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` (Agents Overview section)\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/SKILL.md`\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/default-development-flow.md`\\n\\n**Reference implementation (no changes needed \u2014 pattern source):**\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/agents/ecosystem-researcher.md` \u2014 already implements correct primary-source access via MCP tools; use as the pattern to follow\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None identified. RT-ICA verdict is READY (7 AVAILABLE, 4 DERIVABLE, 0 MISSING). All required information is available or derivable from local codebase inspection without external blockers.\\n- Blocks: Any feature work that runs `add-new-feature` for a backlog item with research artifacts pointing to external sources. The most recently observed instance is backlog item #2241 (codemod-runner skill), but the gap applies to all future features in this category.\\n- Related: Backlog item #2241 \u2014 the observed production instance that triggered this item's creation. No formal dependency relationship; #2241 is already complete (the gap was not caught before the skill was built).\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 rationale:\\n\\n- The fix is purely additive: new process steps and updated philosophy language in agent instruction files. No code changes, no schema migrations, no API changes.\\n- The MCP tools required (`mcp__Ref__ref_read_url`, `mcp__exa__web_search_exa`) are already declared in the agent tool lists \u2014 the capability is present, only the instructions are absent. No tooling work is required.\\n- The reference implementation (`ecosystem-researcher.md`) already shows the exact pattern to follow \u2014 the change can be modeled directly from that file.\\n- The fix surface is wider than a single file: Phase 1 delegation, Phase 3 delegation, `quality_vigilance` preamble, `feature-researcher.md` process and philosophy, `feature-discovery/SKILL.md` in plugin-creator, and a set of documentation files. Each individual change is small, but there are multiple files across two plugins.\\n- No automated tests exist for agent instruction behavior, so verification is manual (observable output inspection against the Acceptance Criteria). This adds some validation effort.\\n- Documentation updates (workflow diagram, plan-artifact-lifecycle, CLAUDE.md, router skill) are mechanical once the agent instruction changes are complete.\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [ ] MINOR: feature-researcher.md Step 2.5 loop treats resource_url and github_url symmetrically \u2014 spec \u00a72.7 prescribes ordered fallback (resource_url first, github_url as fallback when primary fails) (reported by code-reviewer on QG T1)\\n- [ ] MINOR: plan-artifact-lifecycle.md:63 uses backtick inline code for file path instead of markdown link \u2014 violates repo file reference standard (reported by code-reviewer on QG T1)\\n- [ ] MINOR: Phase 1 delegation prompt in add-new-feature/SKILL.md says \\\"log a warning\\\" without specifying `## Research Source Notes` section name prescribed in spec \u00a72.2 (reported by code-reviewer on QG T1)\\n- [ ] MINOR: Phase 3 delegation prompt has same missing section name directive \u2014 architect agent receives no guidance on where to log the warning (reported by code-reviewer on QG T1)\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n\\n**Rationale**: The add-new-feature pipeline executes exactly as designed \u2014 feature-researcher receives a research artifact and adapts from it. The system did not break; the design is incomplete. There is no instruction, validation step, or quality gate requiring agents to (1) extract resource_url from research artifact frontmatter, (2) fetch the primary source, and (3) verify the summary's completeness before adapting. Without this guard, agents inherit information loss and staleness from the research summary layer. The fix is adding the missing guard (a pipeline instruction to feature-researcher and architecture spec agents), not correcting any broken code.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: N/A\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Agents adapt from research summaries without checking primary sources, inheriting information loss and staleness \u2192 Agents fetch primary source URLs from research artifact frontmatter, verify source structure and currency, and adapt from authoritative upstream sources\\n\\n## Observed Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe `add-new-feature` Phase 1 (feature-researcher) and Phase 3 (architecture spec) pipeline, plus the `feature-researcher` agent, have no step that instructs agents to fetch `resource_url` from research artifact frontmatter before adapting external content. Agents treat local research summaries as authoritative sources rather than as discovery artifacts pointing to primary sources.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBacklog item #2241 (codemod-runner skill). Implementation agents adapted from `research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md` \u2014 a research-curator summary. The research frontmatter contained two unused primary source URLs:\\n- `resource_url: https://github.com/ComposioHQ/awesome-codex-skills/tree/master/codebase-migrate`\\n- `github_url: https://github.com/ComposioHQ/awesome-codex-skills`\\n\\nNeither was fetched. The resulting skill reflects the summary's abstractions rather than the full structure, examples, and edge cases present in the original SKILL.md.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Specific Gaps Identified By Audit 2026 05 22\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Primary source access**: Phase 1 delegates to feature-researcher with `artifact_read(..., artifact_type=\\\"research\\\")` but no instruction to extract `resource_url` from frontmatter or fetch it. The `prior_artifacts` block also gives no such guidance.\\n- **No distinction between summary and source**: The pipeline treats research artifacts as authoritative without acknowledging they are summaries of external content.\\n- **Citation following absent**: Neither feature-researcher nor architect is instructed to follow URLs cited in research artifacts to verify currency or completeness before adapting content.\\n- **No online best practices search in Phase 3**: The Architecture Spec delegation has no step to search the web for current best practices before designing. The Python CLI design-spec agent has no WebSearch directive.\\n- **Quality vigilance is local-only**: The \\\"verify before asserting\\\" / \\\"cite sources\\\" guidance in quality_vigilance applies to local `file:line` references only \u2014 not to external URLs in research frontmatter.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSession observation \u2014 2026-05-22, codemod-runner (#2241) implementation review\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:5cfa047f7855a61f05e9c981207ec2eb -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fact Check Results For Issue 2405\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Item**: \\\"Planning pipeline lacks primary-source access: agents adapt from research summaries instead of fetching upstream sources\\\"\\n\\n### Summary\\nAll six claims are **VERIFIED** through direct examination of source files. The planning pipeline (add-new-feature skill) and its delegated agents (feature-researcher, python-cli-design-spec) contain no explicit instructions to extract and follow external resource URLs from research artifacts or to search for current best practices from online sources before designing or implementing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 1: VERIFIED\\n**Claim**: \\\"Phase 1 delegates to feature-researcher with artifact_read(..., artifact_type='research') but no instruction to extract resource_url from frontmatter or fetch it\\\"\\n\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 110-112\\n- Content: \\\"If research artifacts exist for this issue, read them via artifact_read(issue_number={issue}, artifact_type=\\\"research\\\") before starting discovery \u2014 they contain prior investigation findings that should be incorporated.\\\"\\n- Finding: The delegation prompt instructs reading research artifacts but contains NO directive to extract or follow the `resource_url` field from artifact frontmatter.\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` lines 73-87 (\\\"Training Data as Hypothesis\\\" section)\\n- Finding: Feature-researcher instructions include \\\"Verify before asserting\\\" and \\\"Cite sources\\\" but these refer exclusively to local file:line citations, not external URLs in research artifact frontmatter.\\n\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 2: VERIFIED\\n**Claim**: \\\"The pipeline treats research artifacts as authoritative without acknowledging they are summaries of external content\\\"\\n\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 110-112, 336-338 (Phase 1 and Phase 3 delegations)\\n- Content: Both phases refer to research artifacts as \\\"prior investigation findings\\\" with no qualification that they are summaries of external sources.\\n- Counterevidence examined: `research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md` lines 1-10 shows research files DO contain `resource_url` field (line 5: \\\"resource_url: https://github.com/ComposioHQ/...\\\"), confirming research artifacts derive from external sources.\\n- Finding: The pipeline refers to research artifacts as \\\"prior investigation findings\\\" but does NOT acknowledge they originate from and summarize external sources found at `resource_url`.\\n\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 3: VERIFIED\\n**Claim**: \\\"Citation following absent: neither feature-researcher nor architect is instructed to follow URLs cited in research artifacts to verify currency or completeness before adapting content\\\"\\n\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` lines 85-86\\n- Content: \\\"Cite sources - Reference file:line for all claims about the codebase\\\"\\n- Finding: Feature-researcher's citation discipline applies to LOCAL file:line citations only, not external URLs.\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 333-340 (Phase 3 architect delegation)\\n- Content: Architect delegation reads feature context and research artifacts but contains NO instruction to verify currency by following resource_url.\\n\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 4: VERIFIED\\n**Claim**: \\\"No online best practices search in Phase 3: the Architecture Spec delegation has no step to search the web for current best practices before designing\\\"\\n\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 319-347 (Phase 3 \\\"Architecture Spec\\\" delegation prompt template)\\n- Content: Delegation directs reading artifacts and design task, but contains NO instruction to search the web or run WebSearch for current best practices.\\n- Domain skill injection (lines 305-314) loads local skills for schema context only, not online best practices.\\n\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 5: VERIFIED\\n**Claim**: \\\"Quality vigilance is local-only: the 'verify before asserting' / 'cite sources' guidance in quality_vigilance applies to local file:line references only \u2014 not to external URLs in research frontmatter\\\"\\n\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 101-107 (shared preamble quality_vigilance block)\\n- Content: \\\"Point out duplication, contradictions, statements of fact without citation\\\" \u2014 framed around local consistency, not external currency.\\n- Source: `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` lines 85-86\\n- Content: \\\"Cite sources - Reference file:line for all claims about the codebase\\\"\\n- Finding: The \\\"Verify before asserting\\\" and \\\"Cite sources\\\" guidance explicitly scopes to local codebase claims (file:line citations), not external URLs in research artifact frontmatter.\\n\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 6: VERIFIED\\n**Claim**: \\\"The Python CLI design-spec agent has no WebSearch directive\\\"\\n\\n**Evidence**:\\n- Source: `plugins/python3-development/agents/python-cli-design-spec.md` (complete file, 89 lines)\\n- Frontmatter tools (line 4): includes `mcp__exa__web_search_exa` in available tools\\n- Instructions (lines 1-89): Describe architecture design process, reference files to load, sections to produce, but contain NO explicit directive to search the web for best practices as part of the design workflow.\\n- Finding: While the agent has WebSearch capability in its tools, the instructions do NOT explicitly tell it to search for best practices.\\n\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED \u2713\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Overall Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**All six claims are VERIFIED through primary-source inspection.**\\n\\nThe planning pipeline systematically lacks explicit instructions for agents to:\\n1. Extract and follow external URLs from research artifact frontmatter\\n2. Verify the currency and completeness of research-derived content\\n3. Search the web for current best practices as part of design and implementation\\n4. Apply citation discipline to external sources (resource_url fields)\\n\\nThis represents a **systematic gap in the pipeline's guidance on primary-source access** \u2014 agents are directed to read research artifacts but not to validate them against their upstream sources or to supplement local analysis with current external information.\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Citation\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Sources examined**:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` (accessed 2026-05-22)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/feature-researcher.md` (accessed 2026-05-22)\\n- `plugins/python3-development/agents/python-cli-design-spec.md` (accessed 2026-05-22)\\n- `research/skill-generation-tools/composio-codebase-migrate.md` (accessed 2026-05-22)\\n\\n**Verified by**: Haiku 4.5 fact-checker agent on 2026-05-22\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"40f265b17ac00725df1f8f7f39951646c6a992ae284daef5d670943a0aaa4586\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCQYaA\"}"}